      "title": "Estate availability over time",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "gridPos": {"h": 6, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 22},
      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "code": {"language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false},
        "content": "### How uptime is calculated (repeatable method)\n\n**Cluster up (sample = 1):** every ClusterOperator reports `Available=1` — `min by (cluster) (cluster_operator_conditions{condition=\"Available\"})`. This folds in API server availability, ClusterVersion operator health, ClusterOperator availability states and control-plane readiness, since each is a ClusterOperator (`kube-apiserver`, `version`, `etcd`, `kube-controller-manager`, ...).\n\n**Node up (sample = 1):** `kube_node_status_condition{condition=\"Ready\",status=\"true\"}`.\n\n**Planned maintenance:** cluster level = ClusterVersion upgrade in progress (`cluster_operator_conditions{name=\"version\",condition=\"Progressing\"}=1`); node level = node cordoned (`kube_node_spec_unschedulable=1`, e.g. during drains/upgrades). Maintenance windows are counted as *up* in the \"excl. planned\" numbers: `clamp_max(up + maintenance, 1)`.\n\n**Uptime % = `avg_over_time(up_signal[$__range:5m])`** — the mean of the 0/1 up signal sampled every 5 minutes over the dashboard time range, so the number always follows the time picker (default: 30 days). Unplanned downtime minutes = `(1 - uptime_excl_planned) * range_seconds / 60`.\n\n*Notes:* metrics must carry a `cluster` label (central Thanos / multi-cluster observability). Detection resolution is 5 minutes — outages shorter than that may be missed. Maintenance not expressed as an upgrade or cordon (e.g. ad-hoc work) is not auto-excluded; use the upgrade annotations to review windows manually.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "9.0.0",
      "title": "Methodology",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 28},
      "id": 101,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Cluster drilldown — $cluster",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
      "description": "0/1 availability signal per selected cluster (all ClusterOperators available), with the planned-maintenance (upgrade) signal overlaid. Blue annotations mark upgrade windows.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {"legend": false, "tooltip": false, "viz": false},
            "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {"type": "linear"},
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {"group": "A", "mode": "none"},
            "thresholdsStyle": {"mode": "off"}
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "max": 1.1,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}]},
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
